ther case, in which we have to show\n<MATH_0094>, is omitted. (It is similar to the\ncase we did.)\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nProof of (3). We have to prove associativity of composition.\nConsider a solid diagram\n<MATH_0095>\n(whose vertical arrows belong to <MATH_0096>)\nwhich gives rise to three composable pairs.\nUsing LMS2 we can choose the dotted arrows making the squares commutative\nand such that the vertical arrows are in <MATH_0097>.\nThen it is clear that the composition of the three pairs\nis the equivalence class of the pair\n<MATH_0098> gotten by composing the\nhorizontal arrows on the bottom row and the vertical arrows\non the right column.\n\n<STRUCT_0008><STRUCT_0009>\nWe leave it to the reader to check the identity axioms.\n<STRUCT_0010>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f036fde5225f5853819306ea697ff8adf6814082fd6655034cf9f7633af6fc96", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04VD:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:8183881d1da2d854ef34daa5b99758b2abcb01ad2ab83a0e27ba142e8cee221f", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p006-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:6d38fe7edfb8b62c37421a912bd8528710492d77b278af759c34fa88788fb01a"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:04VD:proof"], "policy_revision": "git:b33b9b37f1623d49d4030a11f1661dfc29fa2ce4", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:04VB:enumerate/0001", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:04VD:proof/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [], "unit_id": "tag:04VD:statement"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_required_terms": {"catalog_hash": "sha256:899a668e50f3487b37dd8781e9b5a88e3e16d272ad91b4078ac6b9d847935c12", "occurrences": [{"concept": "category", "projection_end": 29, "projection_start": 21, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "category"}, {"concept": "system", "projection_end": 81, "projection_start": 75, "rule": "catalog", "source